claim.claim-text:
receiving, by a computing device (116) and from an image capture device (102), an image (109) of an optically active article (108) that is based on light captured under a particular lighting condition, wherein the optically active article (108) includes at least one security element (132) and an article message (126);
in response to receiving the image (109), determining, by the computing device (116), validation information that is detectable under the particular lighting condition from the at least one security element (132);
determining, by the computing device (116), whether the optically active article (108) is counterfeit based on whether a combination of the article message (126) and the validation information of the at least one security element (132) is valid; and
performing, by the computing device (116) and based on whether the optically active article (108) is counterfeit, one or more operations,
wherein the article message (126) includes one or more encoding units (600) embedded within one or more symbols that comprise the article message (126), the method further comprising:

determining one or more predefined image regions (142) that correspond to security elements (132) for the optically active article (108);
inspecting one or more of the predefined image regions (142) within the image (109) of the optically active article (108); and
determining, based on one or more pixel values in the predefined image regions (142), one or more values that represent the validation information.
